 \"When did Morea start playing for Papua New Guinea?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 71, \"text\": \"Ipi Morea Ipi Morea (born 6 May 1975) is a Papua New Guinean cricketer.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d00\", \"start\": 72, \"end\": 193, \"text\": \"A right-handed batsman and wicket-keeper, he played for the Papua New Guinea national cricket team between 1996 and 2005.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d00\", \"start\": 194, \"end\": 303, \"text\": \"Born in Port Moresby in 1975, Ipi Morea first played for Papua New Guinea in the 1996 ACC Trophy in Malaysia.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d00\", \"start\": 304, \"end\": 437, \"text\": \"This was followed the next year by an appearance in the 1997 ICC Trophy, also in Malaysia and a second ACC Trophy, in Nepal, in 1998.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d00\", \"start\": 438, \"end\": 546, \"text\": \"After this start it would be nearly four years before he next played for Papua New Guinea, returning for the\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 554, \"text\": \"e Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation ( APEC ) Nations Australia Brunei Canada Chile China Hong Kong ¹ Indonesia Japan South Korea Malaysia Mexico New Zealand Papua New Guinea Peru Philippines Russia Singapore Taiwan Thailand United States Vietnam Summits 1989 1990 1991 1992 1993 1994 1995 1996 1997 1998 1999 2000 2001 2002 2003 2004 2005 2006 2007 2008 2009 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015 2016 2017 2018 2019 2020 2021 2022 2023 2024 2025 Other APEC Business Travel Card APEC blue APEC Climate Center APEC Sculpture Garden APEC Youth Science Festival 1 .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d01\", \"start\": 555, \"end\": 597, \"text\": \"A special administrative region of China ,\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 61, \"text\": \"Ipi Morea (born 6 May 1975) is a Papua New Guinean cricketer.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d02\", \"start\": 62, \"end\": 183, \"text\": \"A right-handed batsman and wicket-keeper, he played for the Papua New Guinea national cricket team between 2000 and 2005.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d02\", \"start\": 184, \"end\": 293, \"text\": \"Born in Port Moresby in 1975, Ipi Morea first played for Papua New Guinea in the 2000 ACC Trophy in Malaysia.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d02\", \"start\": 294, \"end\": 427, \"text\": \"This was followed the next year by an appearance in the 2001 ICC Trophy, also in Malaysia and a second ACC Trophy, in Nepal, in 2002.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d02\", \"start\": 428, \"end\": 540, \"text\": \"After this start it would be nearly three years before he next played for Papua New Guinea, returning for the...\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 88, \"text\": \"Vani Morea Vani Vagi Morea (born 13 March 1983) is a former Papua New Guinean cricketer.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d03\", \"start\": 89, \"end\": 153, \"text\": \"Morea is a right-handed batsman who bowls right-arm medium pace.\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d03\", \"start\": 154, \"end\": 182, \"text\": \"He was born in Port Moresby.\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d03\", \"start\": 183, \"end\": 300, \"text\": \"Morea made his debut for Papua New Guinea in the 2009 World Cricket League Division Three, where he played 5 matches.\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d03\", \"start\": 301, \"end\": 386, \"text\": \"He later appeared for Papua New Guinea in the 2011 World Cricket League Division Two.\"}, \"D4S6\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d03\", \"start\": 387, \"end\": 460, \"text\": \"It was in this competition that he made his List A debut against Bermuda.\"}, \"D4S7\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d03\", \"start\": 461, \"end\": 552, \"text\": \"He played a further 5 List A matches in the competition, the last coming against Hong Kong.\"}, \"D4S8\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d03\", \"start\": 553, \"end\": 555, \"text\": \"In\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 103, \"text\": \", for which the report is still awaited for initial presentation to the Prime Minister and Parliament .\"}, \"D5S2\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d04\", \"start\": 104, \"end\": 113, \"text\": \"[ as of ?\"}, \"D5S3\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d04\", \"start\": 114, \"end\": 246, \"text\": \"] [ citation needed ] Gold discovery Traces of gold were first found in 1852 , in pottery from Redscar Bay on the Papuan Peninsula .\"}, \"D5S4\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d04\", \"start\": 247, \"end\": 340, \"text\": \"[ 110 ] Science and technology Papua New Guinea 's National Vision 2050 was adopted in 2009 .\"}, \"D5S5\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0261-d0268b08d705:d04\", \"start\": 341, \"end\": 425, \"text\": \"This has led to the establishment of the Research , Science and Technology Council .\"}, \"D5S6\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"d